 "text": "Hi, how have you been? If you get a lot of value from it, like a cool design with your name lean, then yes. It' also great for weekends away with a partner. You can still ask to drop her on someone else, and one person can earmark it as their friend's. A basic table still beats eating in the sitting room with the cook looking in. Then swanky table would be nice surprise. If you do want her to share, there are basic shared tables that one adult can sit on. Less than an hour, usually.",
